    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "101(10) 2, 102.2, 102.4, 103.1 and 103.2 and Division 119 of the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-101-ss-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(10) If the Minister becomes aware of conduct because of which a\nperson has, under this section, ceased to be an Australian citizen,\nthe Minister:\n\n(a) must give, or make reasonable attempts to give, written\nnotice to that effect to the person:\n\n(i) as soon as practicable; or\n\n(ii) if the Minister makes a determination under\nsubsection (12)—as soon as practicable after the\nMinister revokes the determination (if the Minister does\nso); and\n\n(b) may give notice to that effect to such other persons and at\nsuch time as the Minister considers appropriate.\nNote:\nA person may seek review of the basis on which a notice under this\nsubsection was given in the High Court of Australia under section 75\nof the Constitution, or in the Federal Court of Australia under\nsection 39B of the Judiciary Act 1903.",
      "skos:definition": "(10) If the Minister becomes aware of conduct because of which a\nperson has, under this section, ceased to be an Australian citizen,\nthe Minister:\n\n(a) must give, or make reasonable attempts to give, written\nnotice to that effect to the person:\n\n(i) as soon as practicable; or\n\n(ii) if the Minister makes a determination under\nsubsection (12)—as soon as practicable after the\nMinister revokes the determination (if the Minister does\nso); and\n\n(b) may give notice to that effect to such other persons and at\nsuch time as the Minister considers appropriate.\nNote:\nA person may seek review of the basis on which a notice under this\nsubsection was given in the High Court of Australia under section 75\nof the Constitution, or in the Federal Court of Australia under\nsection 39B of the Judiciary Act 1903.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-10-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-10-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "849d4dcbff3d3f294e377362b26ca3ca1f68562e1e963db6d6a4868cc23d4cd3",
      "skos:note": "Minister must give written notice to a person who has ceased to be an Australian citizen.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-101-ss-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "101(10) 2, 102.2, 102.4, 103.1 and 103.2 and Division 119 of the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(10) If the Minister becomes aware of conduct because of which a\nperson has, under this section, ceased to be an Australian citizen,\nthe Minister:\n\n(a) must give, or make reasonable attempts to give, written\nnotice to that effect to the person:\n\n(i) as soon as practicable; or\n\n(ii) if the Minister makes a determination under\nsubsection (12)—as soon as practicable after the\nMinister revokes the determination (if the Minister does\nso); and\n\n(b) may give notice to that effect to such other persons and at\nsuch time as the Minister considers appropriate.\nNote:\nA person may seek review of the basis on which a notice under this\nsubsection was given in the High Court of Australia under section 75\nof the Constitution, or in the Federal Court of Australia under\nsection 39B of the Judiciary Act 1903."
    },
