          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-16-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f81c53b0df50e0bb5d426f32be23e5d037fdbc8f3bc88947b6245ae36380107b",
      "skos:note": "Minister is not required to consider matters when exercising power."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-101-ss-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "101(16) 2, 102.2, 102.4, 103.1 and 103.2 and Division 119 of the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(16) To avoid doubt, in deciding whether to consider exercising the\npower in subsection (14), the Minister is not required to have\nregard to any of the matters referred to in subsection (17)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-16-norm",
