    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "101(24) 2, 102.2, 102.4, 103.1 and 103.2 and Division 119 of the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-101-ss-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(24) To avoid doubt, a person’s citizenship is taken never to have\nceased under this section because of particular conduct if:\n\n(a) in proceedings under section 75 of the Constitution, or under\nthis Act or another Commonwealth Act, a court finds that the\nperson did not engage in the conduct or have the requisite\nintention under subsection (3) of this section; or\n\n(b) in proceedings under section 75 of the Constitution, or under\nthis Act or another Commonwealth Act, a court finds that the\nperson was not a national or citizen of a country other than\nAustralia at the time of the conduct; or\n\n(c) the Minister makes a determination under subsection (14) in\nrelation to the conduct to exempt the person from the effect\nof this section; or\n\n(d) a declaration under section 35AA is disallowed by either\nHouse of the Parliament, and the person’s citizenship would\nnot have ceased under this section if that declaration had not\nbeen made.",
      "skos:definition": "(24) To avoid doubt, a person’s citizenship is taken never to have\nceased under this section because of particular conduct if:\n\n(a) in proceedings under section 75 of the Constitution, or under\nthis Act or another Commonwealth Act, a court finds that the\nperson did not engage in the conduct or have the requisite\nintention under subsection (3) of this section; or\n\n(b) in proceedings under section 75 of the Constitution, or under\nthis Act or another Commonwealth Act, a court finds that the\nperson was not a national or citizen of a country other than\nAustralia at the time of the conduct; or\n\n(c) the Minister makes a determination under subsection (14) in\nrelation to the conduct to exempt the person from the effect\nof this section; or\n\n(d) a declaration under section 35AA is disallowed by either\nHouse of the Parliament, and the person’s citizenship would\nnot have ceased under this section if that declaration had not\nbeen made.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-24-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-24-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-24-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-24-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-24-logic-diffusion-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "68d52df54913dd92a7bef6114c34775f2f5f1cec0141e1143ce04872bfd0242b",
      "skos:note": "A person's citizenship is not taken to have ceased under this section if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-101-ss-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "101(24) 2, 102.2, 102.4, 103.1 and 103.2 and Division 119 of the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(24) To avoid doubt, a person’s citizenship is taken never to have\nceased under this section because of particular conduct if:\n\n(a) in proceedings under section 75 of the Constitution, or under\nthis Act or another Commonwealth Act, a court finds that the\nperson did not engage in the conduct or have the requisite\nintention under subsection (3) of this section; or\n\n(b) in proceedings under section 75 of the Constitution, or under\nthis Act or another Commonwealth Act, a court finds that the\nperson was not a national or citizen of a country other than\nAustralia at the time of the conduct; or\n\n(c) the Minister makes a determination under subsection (14) in\nrelation to the conduct to exempt the person from the effect\nof this section; or\n\n(d) a declaration under section 35AA is disallowed by either\nHouse of the Parliament, and the person’s citizenship would\nnot have ceased under this section if that declaration had not\nbeen made."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-24-norm",
