      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(10) The Minister does not have a duty to consider whether to exercise\nthe power under subsection (9) in respect of any person, whether\nthe Minister is requested to do so by the person who has ceased to\nbe a citizen under this section, or by any other person, or in any\nother circumstances.",
      "skos:definition": "(10) The Minister does not have a duty to consider whether to exercise\nthe power under subsection (9) in respect of any person, whether\nthe Minister is requested to do so by the person who has ceased to\nbe a citizen under this section, or by any other person, or in any\nother circumstances.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
