    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35-ss-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35(12) Service outside Australia in armed forces of an enemy country or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-35-ss-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(12) If the Minister decides to consider whether to exercise the power in\nsubsection (9), then, in that consideration, the Minister must have\nregard to the following:\n\n(a) the severity of the matters that were the basis for any notice\ngiven in respect of the person under subsection (5), or of\nmatters that would have been the basis for giving a notice in\nrespect of the person under paragraph (5)(a), but for the\noperation of subsection (7);\n\n(b) the degree of threat posed by the person to the Australian\ncommunity;\n\n(c) the age of the person;\n\n(d) if the person is aged under 18—the best interests of the child\nas a primary consideration;\n\n(e) whether the person is being or is likely to be prosecuted in\nrelation to matters referred to in paragraph (a);\n\n(f) the person’s connection to the other country of which the\nperson is a national or citizen and the availability of the rights\nof citizenship of that country to the person;\n\n(g) Australia’s international relations;\n\n(h) any other matters of public interest.",
      "skos:definition": "(12) If the Minister decides to consider whether to exercise the power in\nsubsection (9), then, in that consideration, the Minister must have\nregard to the following:\n\n(a) the severity of the matters that were the basis for any notice\ngiven in respect of the person under subsection (5), or of\nmatters that would have been the basis for giving a notice in\nrespect of the person under paragraph (5)(a), but for the\noperation of subsection (7);\n\n(b) the degree of threat posed by the person to the Australian\ncommunity;\n\n(c) the age of the person;\n\n(d) if the person is aged under 18—the best interests of the child\nas a primary consideration;\n\n(e) whether the person is being or is likely to be prosecuted in\nrelation to matters referred to in paragraph (a);\n\n(f) the person’s connection to the other country of which the\nperson is a national or citizen and the availability of the rights\nof citizenship of that country to the person;\n\n(g) Australia’s international relations;\n\n(h) any other matters of public interest.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35-ss-12-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35-ss-12-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a44238b899441ceab683671782db39706745e955ead5a759b59c12c4ef92dd46",
      "skos:note": "Minister must consider certain factors when deciding to exercise power"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-35-ss-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35(12) Service outside Australia in armed forces of an enemy country or",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(12) If the Minister decides to consider whether to exercise the power in\nsubsection (9), then, in that consideration, the Minister must have\nregard to the following:\n\n(a) the severity of the matters that were the basis for any notice\ngiven in respect of the person under subsection (5), or of\nmatters that would have been the basis for giving a notice in\nrespect of the person under paragraph (5)(a), but for the\noperation of subsection (7);\n\n(b) the degree of threat posed by the person to the Australian\ncommunity;\n\n(c) the age of the person;\n\n(d) if the person is aged under 18—the best interests of the child\nas a primary consideration;\n\n(e) whether the person is being or is likely to be prosecuted in\nrelation to matters referred to in paragraph (a);\n\n(f) the person’s connection to the other country of which the\nperson is a national or citizen and the availability of the rights\nof citizenship of that country to the person;\n\n(g) Australia’s international relations;\n\n(h) any other matters of public interest."
    },
