    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35AB Sections 33AA and 35 do not apply to conduct of Australian",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-35ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "law enforcement or intelligence bodies or in course of\ncertain duties to the Commonwealth\n\n(1) Sections 33AA and 35 do not apply to conduct engaged in by:\n\n(a) a person in the proper performance of a function of an\nAustralian law enforcement or intelligence body; or\n\n(b) a person acting in the course of the person’s duty to the\nCommonwealth in relation to the defence, security or\ninternational relations of Australia.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015\nNo. 166, 2015\n\n(2) In this section:\nAustralian law enforcement or intelligence body means a body,\nagency or organisation of the Commonwealth, or of a State or\nTerritory, that is responsible for, or deals with, law enforcement,\ncriminal intelligence, criminal investigation, fraud, security\nintelligence, foreign intelligence or financial intelligence.",
      "skos:definition": "law enforcement or intelligence bodies or in course of\ncertain duties to the Commonwealth\n\n(1) Sections 33AA and 35 do not apply to conduct engaged in by:\n\n(a) a person in the proper performance of a function of an\nAustralian law enforcement or intelligence body; or\n\n(b) a person acting in the course of the person’s duty to the\nCommonwealth in relation to the defence, security or\ninternational relations of Australia.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015\nNo. 166, 2015\n\n(2) In this section:\nAustralian law enforcement or intelligence body means a body,\nagency or organisation of the Commonwealth, or of a State or\nTerritory, that is responsible for, or deals with, law enforcement,\ncriminal intelligence, criminal investigation, fraud, security\nintelligence, foreign intelligence or financial intelligence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35ab-ss-1"
        },
