    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35A(5) Conviction for terrorism offences and certain other offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-35a-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the Minister makes a determination under subsection (1) because\nof which a person ceases to be an Australian citizen, the Minister:\n\n(a) must give, or make reasonable attempts to give, written\nnotice to that effect to the person:\n\n(i) as soon as practicable; or\n\n(ii) if the Minister makes a determination under\nsubsection (7)—as soon as practicable after the Minister\nrevokes the subsection (7) determination (if the Minister\ndoes so); and\n\n(b) may give notice to that effect to such other persons and at\nsuch time as the Minister considers appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the Minister makes a determination under subsection (1) because\nof which a person ceases to be an Australian citizen, the Minister:\n\n(a) must give, or make reasonable attempts to give, written\nnotice to that effect to the person:\n\n(i) as soon as practicable; or\n\n(ii) if the Minister makes a determination under\nsubsection (7)—as soon as practicable after the Minister\nrevokes the subsection (7) determination (if the Minister\ndoes so); and\n\n(b) may give notice to that effect to such other persons and at\nsuch time as the Minister considers appropriate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f710a3b0e89f185b93ad8b1aa0efa87237af9a3791f42eebb41e987770eaad6",
      "skos:note": "Minister must give written notice to person ceasing Australian citizenship.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-35a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35A(5) Conviction for terrorism offences and certain other offences",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the Minister makes a determination under subsection (1) because\nof which a person ceases to be an Australian citizen, the Minister:\n\n(a) must give, or make reasonable attempts to give, written\nnotice to that effect to the person:\n\n(i) as soon as practicable; or\n\n(ii) if the Minister makes a determination under\nsubsection (7)—as soon as practicable after the Minister\nrevokes the subsection (7) determination (if the Minister\ndoes so); and\n\n(b) may give notice to that effect to such other persons and at\nsuch time as the Minister considers appropriate."
    },
