    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35A(3) Conviction for terrorism offences and certain other offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, a notice given to a person under paragraph 33AA(10)(a),\n35(5)(a) or 35A(5)(a) must not contain information, or content of a\ndocument, if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015\nNo. 166, 2015\n\n(a) the information or content includes any operationally\nsensitive information (within the meaning of the Independent\nNational Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010); or\n\n(b) the disclosure of the information or content would or might\nprejudice:\n\n(i) the security, defence or international relations of\nAustralia; or\n\n(ii) the performance by a law enforcement or security\nagency (within the meaning of the Independent National\nSecurity Legislation Monitor Act 2010) of its functions;\nor\n\n(c) the disclosure of the information or content would or might\nendanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(d) the disclosure of the information or content would be likely\nto be contrary to the public interest for any other reason.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) However, a notice given to a person under paragraph 33AA(10)(a),\n35(5)(a) or 35A(5)(a) must not contain information, or content of a\ndocument, if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015\nNo. 166, 2015\n\n(a) the information or content includes any operationally\nsensitive information (within the meaning of the Independent\nNational Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010); or\n\n(b) the disclosure of the information or content would or might\nprejudice:\n\n(i) the security, defence or international relations of\nAustralia; or\n\n(ii) the performance by a law enforcement or security\nagency (within the meaning of the Independent National\nSecurity Legislation Monitor Act 2010) of its functions;\nor\n\n(c) the disclosure of the information or content would or might\nendanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(d) the disclosure of the information or content would be likely\nto be contrary to the public interest for any other reason.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "779412dbd136d56da858bb323950b36a1f10eb4e1e05ccf3d63842c4003ef2f7",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of certain information is prohibited in notices. Australian citizenship is a condition for the application of subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35A(3) Conviction for terrorism offences and certain other offences",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, a notice given to a person under paragraph 33AA(10)(a),\n35(5)(a) or 35A(5)(a) must not contain information, or content of a\ndocument, if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015\nNo. 166, 2015\n\n(a) the information or content includes any operationally\nsensitive information (within the meaning of the Independent\nNational Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010); or\n\n(b) the disclosure of the information or content would or might\nprejudice:\n\n(i) the security, defence or international relations of\nAustralia; or\n\n(ii) the performance by a law enforcement or security\nagency (within the meaning of the Independent National\nSecurity Legislation Monitor Act 2010) of its functions;\nor\n\n(c) the disclosure of the information or content would or might\nendanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(d) the disclosure of the information or content would be likely\nto be contrary to the public interest for any other reason."
    },
