    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-2-sec-51c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51C Briefing of Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015#sch-2-sec-51c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "Security\n\n(1) This section applies if any of the following events occurs:\n\n(a) the Minister gives or unsuccessfully attempts to give a notice\nunder paragraph 33AA(10)(a) or 35(5)(a);\n\n(b) the Minister gives or unsuccessfully attempts to give a notice\nunder paragraph 35A(5)(a);\n\n(c) the Minister makes a determination under\nsubsection 33AA(12), 35(7) or 35A(7).\n\n(2) The Minister must, as soon as practicable after the occurrence of\nthe event, inform the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nIntelligence and Security in writing.\n\n(3) Before the later of:\n\n(a) the end of 20 sittings days of the House of Representatives\nafter the occurrence of the event; and\n\n(b) the end of 20 sittings days of the Senate after the occurrence\nof the event;\nthe Minister must, if requested to do so by the Parliamentary Joint\nCommittee on Intelligence and Security, arrange for the Committee\nto be briefed on the event.\n\n(4) The briefing may be done orally or in writing.\n\n(5) The briefing must include details of the following:\n\n(a) for an event mentioned in paragraph (1)(a):\n\n(i) the matters that are the basis for the notice; and\n\n(ii) whether the Minister has rescinded the notice and\nexempted the person to whom the notice related from\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015\nNo. 166, 2015\n\nthe effect of the section in relation to the matters that\nwere the basis for the notice;\n\n(b) for an event mentioned in paragraph (1)(b):\n\n(i) the matters that are the basis for the determination under\nsubsection 35A(1) to which the notice relates;\n\n(ii) whether the Minister has revoked under\nsubsection 35A(8) the determination to which the notice\nrelates; and\n\n(c) for an event mentioned in paragraph (1)(c)—the matters that\nare the basis for the determination.\nIndependent National Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010",
      "skos:definition": "Security\n\n(1) This section applies if any of the following events occurs:\n\n(a) the Minister gives or unsuccessfully attempts to give a notice\nunder paragraph 33AA(10)(a) or 35(5)(a);\n\n(b) the Minister gives or unsuccessfully attempts to give a notice\nunder paragraph 35A(5)(a);\n\n(c) the Minister makes a determination under\nsubsection 33AA(12), 35(7) or 35A(7).\n\n(2) The Minister must, as soon as practicable after the occurrence of\nthe event, inform the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nIntelligence and Security in writing.\n\n(3) Before the later of:\n\n(a) the end of 20 sittings days of the House of Representatives\nafter the occurrence of the event; and\n\n(b) the end of 20 sittings days of the Senate after the occurrence\nof the event;\nthe Minister must, if requested to do so by the Parliamentary Joint\nCommittee on Intelligence and Security, arrange for the Committee\nto be briefed on the event.\n\n(4) The briefing may be done orally or in writing.\n\n(5) The briefing must include details of the following:\n\n(a) for an event mentioned in paragraph (1)(a):\n\n(i) the matters that are the basis for the notice; and\n\n(ii) whether the Minister has rescinded the notice and\nexempted the person to whom the notice related from\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015\nNo. 166, 2015\n\nthe effect of the section in relation to the matters that\nwere the basis for the notice;\n\n(b) for an event mentioned in paragraph (1)(b):\n\n(i) the matters that are the basis for the determination under\nsubsection 35A(1) to which the notice relates;\n\n(ii) whether the Minister has revoked under\nsubsection 35A(8) the determination to which the notice\nrelates; and\n\n(c) for an event mentioned in paragraph (1)(c)—the matters that\nare the basis for the determination.\nIndependent National Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-2-sec-51c-ss-1"
        },
